{"id":"fact-example-001","type":"code_quirk","fact":"Example: The UserService caches results for 5 minutes, so updates may not appear immediately in queries.","recommendation":"Use cache invalidation after writes, or query with { fresh: true } option.","confidence":"medium","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"discovered during debugging","date":"2026-01-15"}],"tags":["caching","user-service"],"affectedFiles":["src/lib/services/user.service.ts"],"affectedServices":["UserService"],"createdAt":"2026-01-15T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-15T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"fact-post-with-revision-shape","type":"code_quirk","fact":"PostWithRevision extends Post with revisions: PostRevision[] array, NOT flat content/revisionNumber fields. Latest content is accessed via currentPost.revisions[0]?.content.","recommendation":"When displaying post content, always access through the revisions array. Use optional chaining since revisions could be empty.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #16 implementation","date":"2026-04-12"}],"tags":["types","posts","revisions","shared-package"],"affectedFiles":["packages/shared/src/types/post.ts","packages/client/src/**/*.vue"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-12T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-12T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"fact-migration-001-search-infrastructure","type":"code_quirk","fact":"packages/server/src/db/migrations/001_initial-schema.sql already ships the complete search infrastructure: pg_trgm + unaccent extensions (lines 4-5), forge_search text-search configuration with english_stem + unaccent (lines 7-9), posts.search_vector tsvector column (line 35), GIN indexes on search_vector and title trgm (lines 121-122), the update_search_vector trigger weighting title A / latest-revision content B / tag names C (lines 129-157), and refresh triggers on post_revisions and post_tags (lines 238-259).","recommendation":"Any future work on search features — filtering, ranking, autocomplete — should verify this existing infrastructure rather than re-create it. A new migration is only needed when *extending* the vector (e.g., adding comment bodies to the mix). For a new search endpoint, use plainto_tsquery('forge_search', $1) and ts_rank(search_vector, query) without any additional DB setup.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #3 search implementation","date":"2026-04-13"}],"tags":["postgresql","search","migrations","tsvector","pg_trgm","pre-existing"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/db/migrations/001_initial-schema.sql","packages/server/src/db/queries/search.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"fact-health-endpoint-path","type":"code_quirk","fact":"The Forge server's health endpoint is mounted at GET /api/health (not /health). The health route is registered via app.register(healthRoutes) — no prefix is passed, but the /api prefix originates from how the route is declared in packages/server/src/routes/health.ts.","recommendation":"When polling for server readiness (CI workflows, local dev scripts, external monitors, documentation), use http://localhost:3001/api/health. Expected body: {\"status\":\"ok\"}.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #28 CI workflow + subagent corrections","date":"2026-04-13"}],"tags":["routing","health","ci","monitoring"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/routes/health.ts",".github/workflows/bruno-regression.yml"],"affectedServices":["health-check"],"createdAt":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"fact-access-token-in-memory-pinia","type":"code_quirk","fact":"The Forge client stores the access token as an in-memory Pinia ref at `packages/client/src/stores/auth.ts:6`: `accessToken = ref<string | null>(null)`. It is NEVER persisted to localStorage or sessionStorage. The refresh token is an HttpOnly cookie scoped to `/api/auth/refresh` (server-set). On boot, `packages/client/src/lib/restore-session.ts:13-41` calls `/api/auth/refresh` to rehydrate the in-memory token from the cookie. The 401-retry path at `packages/client/src/lib/api.ts:65-67` fires `/api/auth/refresh` only when `response.status === 401 && store.accessToken !== null && url !== '/api/auth/refresh'`.","recommendation":"To test refresh-flow behavior in Playwright, do NOT use `addInitScript` to manipulate localStorage — the access token isn't there. Instead, use `page.route('**/api/posts**', handler, { times: 1 })` (or any authenticated GET) to return 401 once; the `api.ts:65` retry will trigger the refresh. To assert the 401-triggered refresh fired, count requests (boot-time refresh fires too — see related gotcha) and assert `>= 2`. Storage state captured by the auth fixture only persists the refresh_token cookie, not the access token.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #46 WU4 session-refresh design + Fact-2 architecture verification","date":"2026-04-29"}],"tags":["client","auth","pinia","access-token","refresh","architecture"],"affectedFiles":["packages/client/src/stores/auth.ts","packages/client/src/lib/api.ts","packages/client/src/lib/restore-session.ts","e2e/fixtures/auth.ts"],"affectedServices":["auth"],"createdAt":"2026-04-29T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-29T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"quirk-no-zero-revision-state","type":"code_quirk","fact":"Every post auto-creates revision 1 via `createRevisionAtomic` on creation. A 0-revision state is structurally impossible without server-side bypass. Empty-state UI tests must use the only-initial-revision case.","recommendation":"When DoD says 'empty state for posts with no revisions', interpret as 'single-revision (only-initial) state' — the closest observable variant. Document the DoD ambiguity in PR body for reviewer adjudication.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"session","reference":"Issue #47 WU13 list-only-initial-revision","date":"2026-04-29"}],"tags":["revisions","posts","seed","invariants"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/db/queries/revisions.ts","packages/server/src/routes/posts.ts","e2e/specs/revisions/list-only-initial-revision.spec.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-29T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-29T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"quirk-history-page-selection-gates","type":"code_quirk","fact":"`PostHistoryPage.vue` gates RevisionDiffViewer with `selectedIds.length >= 2` and RestoreButton with `selectedIds.length === 1 && !isLatestSelected`. The two gates are mutually exclusive — you cannot show both at the same time with the same selection.","recommendation":"Specs that want a diff to render must select TWO revisions (e.g., revisionItem.nth(0) + .last()). Specs that want the restore button must select ONE non-latest revision. The 'permission' rollback test passes via the no-restore-latest gate (ownership is enforced server-side at posts.ts:594), not the UI's gate.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"session","reference":"Issue #47 WU14+WU15","date":"2026-04-29"}],"tags":["revisions","history","ui-gates"],"affectedFiles":["packages/client/src/pages/PostHistoryPage.vue","e2e/specs/revisions/diff-*.spec.ts","e2e/specs/revisions/rollback-*.spec.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-29T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-29T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"fact-seed-testpost-not-testuser-bookmarked","type":"code_quirk","fact":"In scripts/seed.sql, `c0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000099` (testpost — testuser's fixture post used by Bruno) is testuser-OWNED, but the seeded vote (+1) AND bookmark on it are from `a0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001` (alice), NOT testuser. testuser has ZERO seeded bookmarks anywhere in the database. testuser DOES have one seeded comment on c0…99 (`e0…99`).","recommendation":"E2E specs that assume testuser starts with bookmarks must arrange them via API. Specs asserting empty bookmark state default-true for testuser (subject to cross-worker pollution — see gotcha-cross-worker-reset-state-contention). Specs that assume the cheatsheet has testuser's vote are wrong — testuser has no votes in the seed.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"session","reference":"Issue #48 plan REV 1 — Feasibility reviewer caught the mismatch in REV 1's seed table","date":"2026-04-30"}],"tags":["seed","testuser","bookmarks","votes","e2e-fixtures"],"affectedFiles":["scripts/seed.sql","e2e/specs/bookmarks/**","e2e/specs/voting/**"],"affectedServices":["e2e"],"createdAt":"2026-04-30T18:09:39Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-30T18:09:39Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"fact-assert-can-read-post-returns-boolean","type":"code_quirk","fact":"`assertCanReadPost(post, callerId, reply): boolean` returns false (and writes the 403/404 response) instead of throwing. Idiomatic call site: `if (!assertCanReadPost(post, callerId, reply)) return;`. Do NOT wrap it in try/catch — it never throws. Do NOT use the return value as a truthy authorization predicate without the early-return — code after the call still executes if you forget.","recommendation":"Always pair the call with an early `return` when it returns false. Treat it like Fastify's reply pattern — the response is already written; you must just stop further work on the route.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #50 — /api/playground/run authorization","date":"2026-05-01"}],"tags":["authorization","fastify","posts","convention"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/services/postAuth.ts","packages/server/src/routes/**/*.ts"],"affectedServices":["server"],"createdAt":"2026-05-01T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-01T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"fact-use-posts-fork-post-return-shape","type":"code_quirk","fact":"`usePosts.forkPost(postId)` returns `Promise<string | null>` — the new post's id on success, or `null` on failure. The composable does NOT itself navigate; redirect logic lives in callers (e.g., PlaygroundHeader sends prompt-source forks to `/playground/{newId}` and other content-types to `/posts/{newId}/edit`).","recommendation":"Callers must (1) await the returned id, (2) handle null, (3) decide where to navigate based on the source post's contentType. Do NOT assume forkPost handles routing.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #50 — fork-from-playground UI","date":"2026-05-01"}],"tags":["client","composable","fork","navigation"],"affectedFiles":["packages/client/src/composables/usePosts.ts","packages/client/src/components/playground/PlaygroundHeader.vue"],"affectedServices":["client"],"createdAt":"2026-05-01T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-01T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
